Omission
- [N1] Node-level omission: If the order needs to be cancelled, the process ends. If not, check the quality of the goods. (reason: The explicit cancellation vs. quality-check decision point and its associated end path are completely absent from the model elements.)
- [N2] Omitted trace (input 1): i1:To start the process, begin by supplying the requirement and then documenting it. -> i2:If the order is received via fax -> i4:Once the Excel list is complete after a week, send it to the student. -> i5:Upon receiving the Excel list, type the orders into the MS-Access database. -> i6:After typing the orders into the database, ensure that it is completed. -> i7:control the incoming order. At the same time, continue to do the check. -> i8:If the order is correct, release it. -> i9:Send the Excel list to the student and upon receiving it, continue with the process. -> i11:If the order is worth less than 5.000 €, release it. -> i15:Once the order is received by PPC, they will initiate production. -> i16:If the issue cannot be solved, cancel the order. If the issue can be solved, release the order. -> i18:If the issue can be solved, release the order. -> i19:After PPC initiates production, the goods will be produced. -> i20:If the order needs to be cancelled, the process ends.
